  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One. The project has since received executive approval for a total budget of $2 million. Key milestones include the addition of five new team members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture (onboarded September 10th), and the expansion of the team with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. Initial findings presented by Tom on August 5th indicated a potential 20% efficiency increase using AI algorithms. The project reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, leading to a design phase completion and the start of the development phase next month, led by Omar Jensen. Recent updates from Neil highlight a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, with a detailed report scheduled for the staff meeting on November 20th. The next phase involves user interface enhancements planned to commence in October."
